  "content": "Dual-binary architecture: the CLI binary (cmd/main.go) is what `claude mcp add` registers and Claude Code/Codex/Cursor spawn over stdio. The Wails desktop app (cmd/app) is the human-facing console - browse memories, edit them, trigger dreams, manage config. Both share the same SQLite DB (~/.local/share/memorable-mcp/memories.db) and config.toml. As of 2026-05-26, the desktop ALSO serves MCP over HTTP at :47823/mcp from the same Server instance, so `make start` is the single command for everything - no separate `make serve` process required.",
